Well, I've compiled NetHack myself, so I can answer my own original 
question now.  It doesn't take that much longer to compile than NH 3.0.
The full 3.1 make took under 2 hours, and that includes a few stops and 
recompiles due to nmake problems.  Now that I have the new nmake, things 
should be smoother & faster.  Also, this was while using emx GCC instead of 
MS C6, and supposedly GCC is a slower compiler than MSC (but produces 
faster code).  So, it actuality, 3.1 should only be about twice as long
to compile for a full build (at least for me...).  That's not too 
unmanagable.
